{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["Out of Asher his bread is rich — because from Asher they would bring olive oil and fry their food in oil. And so Moshe said: Blessed be Asher above sons. Let him be favored by his brothers — because he dips his foot in oil." "And he yields royal delicacies — a tribute of oil the kings of Israel would levy from him, to anoint themselves with it to soften their flesh, as we say in Menaḥot: 'an unpresented olive oil' — oil that the distributor did not bring a third. And why do they anoint with it? Because it removes the hair and softens the flesh. As in: ״היתה לי עדנה בשר חלק״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {1 "The rabbinic passage is rendered hyper-literally; the Aramaic term אנפיקונון (' distributor/steward') is translated as 'distributor.' The unaddressed Scriptural and rabbinic quotations are left unaddressed as in the original."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:49.296507630Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}